Subject: screenreader: save the setting in setEnabled(), as toggle() does

Without systemd the module keeps whether Orca runs in kaccessrc and starts
it at login only when that file says so. toggle() saves the change;
setEnabled(), which System Settings and other D-Bus callers use, changed
only the value in memory, so its choice was lost at the next login.

--- a/kded/screenreader/screenreader.cpp
+++ b/kded/screenreader/screenreader.cpp
@@ -156,6 +156,7 @@
         }
     } else {
         m_settings.setEnabled(enabled);
+        m_settings.save();
 
         if (enabled) {
             startScreenReaderFallback();
